// A condition that is never true, so the lines under it never run.

@var $x = true

== kitchen.door
@if false
//  ^^^^^ PIB3040
    This never runs.
@if 1 > 2
//  ^^^^^ PIB3040
    This never runs.
@if not true
//  ^^^^^^^^ PIB3040
    This never runs.
@if $x
    This runs sometimes.
@elif false and $x
//    ^^^^^^^^^^^^ PIB3040
    This never runs.
@if $x and false
//  ^^^^^^^^^^^^ PIB3040
    This never runs, whatever `$x` is.

// Must not trigger

@if true
    A condition that is always true has nothing after it to report.
@if $x
    This can change.
@else
    So can this.
This line says {if false}nothing{else}something{/if}.
